       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg once daily is five times the maximum recommended dose, which is 10 mg once daily. Even for a patient with normal kidney and liver function, that dose risks severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. The usual adult starting dose is 5 mg daily.\n\nIt's also possible the dose was meant to be 5 mg or 10 mg, or there may be a different intended medication. Before any order goes in, a licensed prescriber on the medicine service should confirm the intended drug and dose. Since you're not a clinician, I'd also check whether your hospital's policy allows non-prescribers to enter medication orders at all.\n\nIf a prescriber confirms the intended dose, send me the drug, dose, route, and frequency and I'll enter it. If you'd like, I can enter amlodipine 5 mg by mouth once daily, but only once a prescriber has approved that dose."
